    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40707" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">reddĭtĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		reddo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a giving back</i>, <i>returning.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Jucunditatis,
					<i><span class="en">Vulg. Ecclus. 1, 29</span></i>: rationis,
			i. e. <i>rendering a reason</i>, Aug. Civ. Dei, 21,
			7.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A repetition</i>, <i>recurrence</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">orationis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart. Cap. 5, § 533</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			Rhet. t. t., Gr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπόδοσις,</span>
			<i>the consequent clause</i>, <i>the
				apodosis</i>, <i><span class="en">Quint. 8, 3, 77</span></i>; <i><span class="en">79</span></i>; <i><span class="en">80</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Aus. Idyll. 12</span></i> pr.</div>
